cannot write a frame whose columns have different lengths

Assumption: `with_column` does not check that its column has the frame's row
count, so a frame whose columns disagree is reachable. The CSV writer must
refuse it loudly. It assembles rows by zipping the per-column cell lists
together, and a zip alone would truncate every row to the shortest column and
write a short file with no diagnostic, so this case guards a silent-data-loss
path rather than a type rule. A pass here means the writer started truncating.
